{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792694704,"nonce":"e6c5KZ9GdsA9qo7HCwFQHBwwICg=","message":"Class design proposal (research only, unverified by build; file:line references are from a read-only code survey and need checking before use)\n\nAlready in Zyntax: TypedClass/TypedField/TypedMethod/TypedConstructor/TypedMethodCall exist; no New/this/super expression. Reference structs get a header word (TypeMetadata.is_reference, object_header.rs). lower_class emits free functions Class_method and does no allocation; extends/implements/abstract are ignored by the compiler. Python (zyntax_python classes.rs/types.rs) is the model: @reference struct + empty TypedClass, generated C$new, methods as free functions C$m, a $class tag and tag-switch dispatcher. Drop glue (drop_glue.rs) frees reference fields recursively but assumes unique ownership and runs only with ZYNTAX_DROP_GLUE=1; it ignores Optional\u003cNamed\u003e (tagged union) fields.\n\nTrue gaps: shared virtual dispatch, static-field lowering, module-level drop-glue flag, nullable class reference representation, cycles (need a collector).\n\nSlice 1 (in): non-generic class without extends, nominal TypeId per class, constructor, parameter properties, field initializers in order, instance methods as static calls C$m(this, ...), new (C$new: zeroed struct then init), this, static methods, access modifiers/readonly as compile-time checks.\nSlice 1b (benchmarks): class-typed owning fields, C | null as a niche pointer, arrays of class elements.\nOut (explicit Unsupported): extends/super/implements/abstract, static fields, accessors, #private, class expressions, generics, instanceof, this captured by closures, exported classes.\nBenchmarks: nbody needs slice 1 + arrays of class; binary-trees needs 1b; richards and deltablue need shared back-references and stay Unsupported until f29ca38.\n\nOwnership: a reference field is a unique owning edge; new/call results are fresh; a field read is a borrowed alias. A parameter stored into a field is Owned and the call site may pass only a fresh value; otherwise Unsupported. This forbids n.next = n, so runtime cycles cannot be built and glue is safe. this is Borrowed; storing this into another object is Unsupported. Keep Collector::None.\n\nDecisions needed: D1 fold reference-valued fields (5f1038e) into slice 1b or ship scalar-only classes first; D2 drop glue as a module/runtime flag instead of an env var (shared-compiler change); D3 niche pointer vs Type::Optional for T | null (niche recommended, glue handles it); D4 virtual dispatch: frontend-local tag switch or extract Python's into a shared crate; D5 richards/deltablue as explicit gaps until f29ca38 (MarkSweep is unsafe with interpreter-held values); D6 returned field projections are not modelled by params_returned_by, so a borrowed field returned through a call could outlive its owner: add a regression test or reject; D7 the 579 class rows stay UNSUPPORTED/FAIL until real.","files":null}]}